By Fourier inversion (relation \eqref{fourinv}), we have  egin{align} \sum_{\substack{n < X\n\equiv c_d \imod d}}\mathfrak{f}(n)1_{\mathcal{A}_r}(n+s) = \dfrac{1}{X}\sum_{0\leq t<X}\widehat{1}_{\mathcal{A}_r} igg(\dfrac{t}{X} igg)\widehat{\mathfrak{f}}_{d, c_d} igg(\dfrac{-t}{X} igg)e igg(\dfrac{-st}{X} igg), \end{align} where $\widehat{1}_{\mathcal{A}_r}$ and $\widehat{\mathfrak{f}}_{d, c_d}$ are given by \eqref{Arfourier} and \eqref{Fourf}, respectively. We consider the parameter $C>0$ to be chosen later. Then we dissect the fractions $t/X$ with $t\in [0, X)\cap \mathbb{Z}$ into two sets: major arcs $\mathfrak{M}$ and minor arcs $\mathfrak{m}$ (see Section ef{Setup} for definition of these two sets). We may now use Proposition ef{PropMajArc} to estimate the major arcs $\mathfrak{M}$ contribution. We will show that  egin{align} \sum_{\substack{d\leq D\(d, b)=1}}&{\sigma}(d) igg(\dfrac{1}{X}\sum_{\substack{0\leq t<X\t\in \mathfrak{M}}}\widehat{1}_{\mathcal{A}_r} igg(\dfrac{t}{X} igg)\widehat{\mathfrak{f}}_{d, c_d} igg(\dfrac{-t}{X} igg)e igg(\dfrac{-st}{X} igg)-\dfrac{ \lambda_{d}}{\varphi(d)}\dfrac{b}{\varphi(b)}\sum_{\substack{n< X}}1_{\mathcal{A}_r}(n) igg)\ll \dfrac{X^\zeta}{(\log X)^C}. \end{align} For brevity, let us denote  egin{align} 
