otag &\ll X^{\zeta}  igg(\dfrac{(\log X)^{C'}}{(\log X)^{C(\omega/2-\alpha_b)}} + \dfrac{X^{\alpha_b}(\log X)^{C'}}{X^{\omega/2}} igg)(\log X)^2\ll \dfrac{X^{\zeta}}{(\log X)^{A}}, \end{align} where we have chosen $C=(A + C' +2)/(\omega/2-\alpha_b)$. Note that $\alpha_b$ goes to $0$ as $bightarrow \infty$ (see the relation \eqref{alphab}). In particular, since the base $b$ is sufficiently large, we have $\omega/2> \alpha_b$. Along with \eqref{Thm7eq2}, this completes the proof of Theorem ef{Thm G}.
